<card id="c" title="Zla Kolata and Prokletije: 300 Euros There and Back">
<do type="prev" label="Back"><prev/></do>
<p>The ride to Gusinje took four hours. The farther we got from Podgorica, the more beautiful it became: the mountains higher and higher, fewer and fewer cars on the road.</p>
<p><b>4. Gusinje and day 0 at the campsite in Vusanje</b></p>
<p>The bus arrived in Gusinje on time. It was a very warm but not hot day. Straight off the bus I went to the supermarket to stock up on food and water for the first days: I had no idea what to expect from the campsite. I bought a few cans of beef goulash, a can of tuna salad, pasta, onions and bananas, plus a couple of bottles of water and one beer.</p>
<p>I loaded everything into my backpack and a tote bag and set off for Vusanje. The backpack now weighed about 25 kg, but thanks to its load-distribution system it didn&apos;t feel too heavy.</p>
